From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:22:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/21] media: i2c: Add Samsung S5KGD1SP image sensor driver

New driver for the Titan 2 front camera, written from a sensor
specification: one mode, 3280x2464@30 on 4 D-PHY lanes (432 MHz),
RAW10.

On stream start the driver checks the chip ID (0x0841), writes the five
fixed reset writes, waits 24 ms and then the sensor firmware patch (TnP).
The TnP is not part of the driver and is not distributed: the user has to
supply it as /lib/firmware/s5kgd1sp_tnp.bin, loaded with
request_firmware(), a flat array of little-endian u16 { register, value }
pairs written in order.

Controls: exposure (3.., margin 3), analogue gain (code = gain * 32,
1x..16x), vblank, hblank, pixel rate, link frequency, test pattern and
its four colour components (0x0600..0x0608), h/v flip (0x0101, relative
to the mounting of the module), orientation/rotation. Exposure, gain and
frame length updates are wrapped in group hold (0x0104).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
